ing hand\n\nReason: Discarding F2 maintains maximum flexibility in the Dots suit. With B4, B5, B6, B7, B7, B8 remaining, I can form multiple potential winning combinations. I can use B7, B7 as my pair and wait for tiles like B3 (to form B3-B4-B5 + B6-B7-B8), B6 (to form B4-B5-B6 + B6-B7-B8), or B9 (to form B4-B5-B6 + B7-B8-B9). This gives me the best chance to achieve a winning hand with 8+ points.\n\nAnswer: Play F2"}
